title mycelium Purse — one holder's double-spend decided per account by the agreed order (r1)
prompt Continue the agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first past the closed Till arc; open the next Season D crux; send each finished increment to origin and xykj61; stop at custody gates.
think The Till closed the treasury's contested draw over a GLOBAL supply and named, twice, the horizon it left open — per-account balances, the truest double-spend. Lindy-first crux-first, that horizon is the ledger's own next crux (the core state model, what unlocks real accounts), not merely another parallel verdict arc. Chose it over the .kres breach (a rename opens no new capability; crux-first prefers the hard move that opens the rest) and over Puddle (a jump off the productive spine).
think A transfer rides the Cord without editing an elder: sender = the fact's own signer_pk, amount = its amount, recipient = the fact's signed 256-byte body (bound to the sender's signature, so it cannot be redirected). A genesis credit is kind_issue (body = account funded); a transfer is kind_tax (body = recipient). The Purse reuses fold's signed-fact machinery and folds its OWN per-account law over cord.commit's agreed order.
think The honest distinction is the Till's twin per account: the measure is received-so-far[holder], the monotonic cumulative inflow. Overdraws current balance yet amount <= received-so-far = lost a race (lawful no-op spent-out loss); amount > received-so-far = never could pay (refuse whole). Conservation is the new invariant a per-account model earns and the global model could not state — no coin made or destroyed by a move, so balances_sum always == total_issued, asserted at the resolve postcondition and inside balances_sum.
think One additive touch to an elder: fold.verify_fact (pub) exposes the exact signature gate fold_fact already runs, for a resolver that folds a different law over the same signed facts — the same additive shape cord.verify_block/address already set for a Byzantine-aware caller. No elder behavior moved; fold's own selftest re-runs GREEN.
obs Crux demo: genesis credits 100 to Alice; Alice signs two 100-transfers (to Bob, to Carol) at the same round — a real equivocation cord.add admits as two distinct-hash blocks. commit tie-breaks by block hash (same author+round), so the earlier-sorting transfer moves the coins and the later faces an emptied purse. Winner paid 100, loser's recipient 0, Alice 0 (spent once, not twice); loss is Alice's for 100, lawful (100<=received 100); conservation holds; purses_equal across both arrivals. Never-could-pay (500>received) → NeverPaid; tampered fact sig → IdentityRefused; a star reserve → StarReserve (honest to own resource, as the Till refused StarTaken); a non-key recipient body → Malformed. Each refuses whole.
obs GREEN first pass; TAME bans clean (purse.rye + fold.rye not in the zero-assert exempt list), width exit 0. Scope stayed narrow: real mint authority, transfer fees, account expiry, and a served Purse are named horizons behind the gates. The Purse opens the third Season D contested-verdict arc (Tenure names · Till supply · Purse accounts), and the first that earns a conservation law.
